A||N||9||Fallman||Engine Oil Coolers||||1||
Z||000000||Fallman||09-25-2001||04:41 PM||||I am wondering about putting an oil cooler on my 86'GT 2.8L 3spd Auto.  I was just wanted some information from anyone who has done this or has any information about it. Also wondering what RPM can be sustained for how long with out damaging the 2.8L for lack of oil.  This is part of the reason for the cooler||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||09-25-2001||04:44 PM||||Correct me if I'm wrong but don't the automatics come  with a tranny cooler already in the rad?  The tranny lines are on the drivers side of the car, at least mine had them there until I did the conversion.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fallman||09-25-2001||04:46 PM||||Yes, you are right. Maybe i should have been more Clear this is An ENGINE Oil Cooler. What did you convert yours to.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jay||09-25-2001||04:51 PM||||Sorry, I misunderstood.  I did the Northstar conversion (see web page in sig).  As far as I know a remote engine oil cooler is simple to do and most any performance shop will carry one, probably even Pep Boys.  If you have the side scoops on your car you could put the cooler in your wheel wells, but I'm NOT speaking from experience.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fierowrecker||09-25-2001||05:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fallman:<BR><B>I am wondering about putting an oil cooler on my 86'GT 2.8L 3spd Auto.  I was just wanted some information from anyone who has done this or has any information about it. Also wondering what RPM can be sustained for how long with out damaging the 2.8L for lack of oil.  This is part of the reason for the cooler</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Fallman!<BR>I have installed oil coolers in the past on Novas and such, but not on a Fiero, as yet...<BR>But it has always been a straight forward bolt on operation...<BR>The instructions may be a little skimpy, but, if you have any auto repair knowledge, you should be fine...<BR>I would run half inch steel lines from the cooler to the engine and then use half inch hydrolic hoses to the adaptor...<BR>Be sure the hoses are hydrolic hoses!!!<BR>You can get the hoses and fittings from tractor supply, county post, or just look under hydrolics in the phone book...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fallman||09-26-2001||12:52 AM||||Thanks for the info i am pretty familiar with the whole auto mechanic scene i rebuilt the engine and transmission myself and am actually headed for wyoming tech as soon as i can get my butt moving. so yeah i understand. i was just looking for advice form people with experience and also feed back on the 2.8 and its short comings so far this is my first fiero, and hopefully not the last.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fierowrecker||09-26-2001||06:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fallman:<BR><B>Thanks for the info i am pretty familiar with the whole auto mechanic scene i rebuilt the engine and transmission myself and am actually headed for wyoming tech as soon as i can get my butt moving. so yeah i understand. i was just looking for advice form people with experience and also feed back on the 2.8 and its short comings so far this is my first fiero, and hopefully not the last.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The short comings of the 2.8...<BR>Too small!!!<BR>Try a 3800...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Joe Torma||09-26-2001||06:19 PM||||The 3400 series motors had a coolant cooled oil cooler.  My motor didn't come with it, but I purchased it to put on.  It basically goes between the block and oil filter.  You need to run 2 lines...one to a plug right nest to the filter on block and one to the water feed line.<P>I can post pics if you want.  I paid about $110.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fallman||09-26-2001||07:31 PM||||I would love a 3.8 out of a Grande National if anyone nows of one but right know money is kind of tight so yeah<P>About the cooler<BR>can i get one of those for a 2.8 and if so where||||reg||1
Z||000009||Joe Torma||09-27-2001||11:14 AM||||Yes, you can get the cooler from any GM dealer and should fit any 3.4/3.1/2.8.  Ask for a 97 Chevy Venture Van oil cooler(3.4L) and make sure you get the bolt-tube thing to put it on(you onscrew the threaded tube that the oil filter screws on to and put the oil cooler on and bolt it on with the new tube.  I'll see if I have the part #s handy <p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-27-2001).]||||reg||1
